WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:08.380
Superhero movies present us with larger-than-life
heroes who overcome impossible odds to save

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.560
the day. The real heroes though are the actors
who don the outfits to bring these comic book

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.289
legends to life… Because the experiences
aren't always so pleasant. Here are some examples

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:23.009
of actors who have put on the super-suits,
but didn't particularly enjoy doing so.

00:00:23.009 --> 00:00:24.150
Andrew Garfield

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:28.150
As the famous webhead in both Amazing Spider-Man
films, Garfield gave us a different look at

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:32.050
Peter Parker. But what Garfield didn't want
us to get a look at was his Spider-Man outfit

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.250
and how uncomfortable and unflattering it
was.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:39.340
"I knew there were paparazzi taking terrible
unflattering shots of my, you know, everything,"

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.020
said Garfield, according to Digital Spy. “The
whole point of wearing a mask is you feel

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.800
free and you can be whatever you want and
you can be witty.”

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.770
But then he was made uncomfortable by the
fact that onlookers were getting butt shots

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:53.890
of him from many, many different angles. That’s
one way to get your Spider Sense tingling.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.690
Chadwick Boseman

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:59.780
As the first, live-action version of Marvel's
Black Panther in Captain America: Civil War,

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.960
Chadwick Boseman had to squeeze into a black
catsuit in 90-degree weather. Boseman talked

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.360
to Cinema Blend about how certain stunts would
be physically demanding because of the suit.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:13.000
"And every time they add a part, I'd be like
'you mean...you just gonna cut off my air

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.080
supply?' Like 'oh okay let me figure out how
to breath like that.'"

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.460
He also talked about how he had to get into
a "Zen space" in order to get through the

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:25.380
difficult stunts, since he'd have sweat rolling
down his body and was unable to scratch itches.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:29.380
You'd think it would have been easy for him,
especially with those Vibranium claws.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:30.960
Scarlett Johansson

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.900
Black Widow might have had red in her ledger,
but Scarlett Johansson had sweat in her socks.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.940
Johansson said in an interview with Nightline
about the first Avengers movie, "It was so

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.280
hot, I would wring out my socks at the end
of the day."

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.190
That's gross, but also it's understandable
considering the fact that her Black Widow

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:48.920
costume was like a wetsuit and wasn't pleasant
in the heat. In fact, it got so hot that she

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.979
actually hallucinated for a bit while filming
a fight scene. Johannson also compared the

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:56.750
multiple costumes she had to tires, because
her stunts would wear each one down until

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:00.170
she needed to replace them. Pulling off all
of those hurricanranas couldn't have been

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.110
easy on those stitches.

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:03.530
Malin Akerman

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:07.840
As sweaty as some actors get in their costumes,
Malin Akerman's experiences in the Silk Spectre

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.030
costume for Watchmen were wholly different.
The skin-tight, black and yellow suit shows

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.940
off her physique while looking pretty badass.
But, according to Maxim, Akerman said that

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.150
the latex costume smelled terrible.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.650
"I thought it was really f***ing hot at first.
Then I tried it on, and I thought it was really

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.880
f***ing uncomfortable. When you take it off,
it smells like a human condom," said Akerman.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:31.480
And with those words, we can never see Watchmen
again without gagging just a little bit.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.340
Olivia Munn

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.760
While donning costumes can empower superheroes,
it's another thing altogether to actually

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:41.230
get into them. Olivia Munn, who played Psylocke
in X-Men: Apocalypse, revealed on Conan that

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:44.620
it took a bit of help to get her into the
character's iconic purple costume. To be more

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.599
specific, it took the help of two women and
a lot of lube to get the outfit on. You'd

00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:51.599
think that having to do that every time you
had to shoot a scene was embarrassing enough,

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:55.099
but the first time she got on set with the
veteran X-Men actors, she actually popped

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:57.599
the crotch on the suit—whoops.

00:02:57.599 --> 00:02:59.090
Rebecca Romijn

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.340
In a 2003 interview with Entertainment Weekly,
Rebecca Romijn talked about how hard it was

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.599
to get the Mystique makeup applied for the
filming of X2: X-Men United. The process involved

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:11.709
four women and a little under eight hours,
effectively souring Romijn's mood as time

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:12.520
went on.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.940
"When I first took this on, they told me it
would take ten hours."

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.520
"Six hours."
"Ten hours!"

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.920
The worst part, however, was the fact that
she was naked under all of the makeup while

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.140
everyone else got to wear outfits. At one
point, director Bryan Singer came into her

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.440
tent while she was bent over a chair and getting
her "crack touched up." She might been painted

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.379
blue, but we're willing to bet her face was
pretty red.

00:03:32.379 --> 00:03:33.680
Margot Robbie

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.800
She may quite literally slay in her Suicide
Squad hot pants, but Margot Robbie was definitely

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.620
not a fan of them. While a lot of folks are
making her Harley Quinn out to be an overtly

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:45.739
sexual piece of eye candy, Robbie said that
Quinn likes the shorts "because they're sparkly

00:03:45.739 --> 00:03:48.849
and fun" and not because she wants guys ogling
her.

00:03:48.849 --> 00:03:49.700
"What?"

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.540
"As Margot, no, I don't like wearing that.
I'm eating burgers at lunchtime, and then

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.730
you go do a scene where you're hosed down
and soaking wet in a white T-shirt, it's so

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.120
clingy and you're self-conscious about it,"
Robbie told The New York Times.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.330
Ben Affleck

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:06.200
Our newest Batman has made it known that he's
not a huge fan of the Batsuit he wore in Batman

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.140
v Superman: Dawn of Justice. While many a
fanboy would love to don the cape and cowl,

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.900
Affleck called it "the most humiliating, ridiculous
thing in the world." According to Total Film,

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.379
this is because the Batsuit was really a motion
capture suit that allowed for greater range

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:22.949
of movement. He even gave a nickname to the
suit and called it his "visual effects pajamas."

00:04:22.949 --> 00:04:25.850
We understand that he might have felt it was
embarrassing to wear the outfit because it

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:30.270
didn't make him feel badass like Batman, but
at least there were no Bat-nipples.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.590
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.940
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which super-suit you think looks the

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:37.699
most uncomfortable...

